---

<BaseLayout title="Always-on Hermes | Dave Coulter" description="A private, always-on Hermes Agent deployment running in a Debian VM on a Proxmox homelab.">
  <header class="project-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Private AI infrastructure</p>
    <h1>Always-on<br />Hermes<span class="signal">.</span></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">A workstation-bound AI agent moved into a private, always-on Debian virtual machine while preserving local desktop control and keeping every remote service off the public internet.</p>
    <div class="project-hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/projects/status/2026-09-24-always-on-hermes-proxmox/">Read the full build notes →</a></div>
    <div class="project-meta"><span class="badge">Proxmox</span><span class="badge">Debian</span><span class="badge">Tailscale</span><span class="badge">2026</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="hermes-signal" aria-labelledby="hermes-signal-title">
    <div class="hermes-signal-bar">
      <span id="hermes-signal-title">Hermes // Nous Research</span>
      <span><i aria-hidden="true"></i> Agent online</span>
    </div>
    <figure class="hermes-portrait">
      <pre aria-hidden="true">{hermesAscii}</pre>
      <figcaption>Source image translated into a 52-column braille-cell portrait.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="hermes-signal-footer" aria-hidden="true">
      <span>Private network</span>
      <span>Debian 13 / Proxmox</span>
      <span>Availability: persistent</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section section-grid">
    <p class="kicker">01 / Overview</p>
    <div class="project-copy"><p>Hermes originally ran only on my Omarchy workstation. I moved its persistent services into a Debian VM on Proxmox so scheduled work, messaging, and remote sessions can continue when the workstation is unavailable.</p><p>The workstation retains a separate local installation for tasks that need direct access to Omarchy, desktop applications, and local files. Tailscale provides the private network boundary between both environments.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section section-grid">
    <p class="kicker">02 / What the project solved</p>
    <div class="project-copy"><ul><li>Preserved conversations, memory, skills, scheduled jobs, source files, Git history, untracked work, and project configuration.</li><li>Separated durable state from regenerable dependencies, caches, environments, and build output.</li><li>Moved messaging through a rollback-safe cutover without running duplicate gateways.</li><li>Kept dashboards, backends, SSH, and integrations private through Tailscale and least-privilege access.</li><li>Retained the local Hermes installation for machine-specific desktop work.</li></ul></div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section section-grid">
    <p class="kicker">03 / Development notes</p>
    <div class="project-copy"><p>The migration was treated as an infrastructure project rather than a file copy. Every major step had a rollback path, and verification checked application state, adapter connectivity, database integrity, permissions, and real outbound delivery—not just whether a process appeared to be running.</p><p>The resulting pattern now guides future homelab integrations: private networking, dedicated credentials, tightly constrained operations, structured health checks, and no public exposure.</p></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hermes-signal {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background:
      linear-gradient(90deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--signal) 4%, transparent) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(color-mix(in srgb, var(--signal) 4%, transparent) 1px, transparent 1px),
      var(--surface);
    background-size: 32px 32px;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 90px color-mix(in srgb, var(--signal) 4%, transparent);
  }

  .hermes-signal::after {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(transparent 50%, rgb(7 7 6 / 18%) 50%);
    background-size: 100% 4px;
    content: '';
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .hermes-signal-bar,
  .hermes-signal-footer {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 700 10px/1.2 var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: .07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hermes-signal-bar {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .hermes-signal-bar span:first-child { color: var(--fg); }

  .hermes-signal-bar i {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    margin-right: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--signal);
    box-shadow: 0 0 12px var(--signal);
  }

  .hermes-portrait {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    margin: 0;
    padding: clamp(34px, 6vw, 78px) 12px 24px;
  }

  .hermes-portrait pre {
    max-width: 100%;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--signal);
    font: 400 clamp(.34rem, 1.08vw, .92rem)/.94 var(--mono);
    text-shadow: 0 0 18px color-mix(in srgb, var(--signal) 22%, transparent);
  }

  .hermes-portrait figcaption {
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 4vw, 44px);
    color: var(--muted);
    font: 700 10px/1.4 var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .hermes-signal-footer {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hermes-signal-bar { align-items: flex-start; }
    .hermes-signal-footer { flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
    .hermes-signal-footer span:not(:first-child)::before {
      margin-right: 7px;
      color: var(--signal);
      content: '↳';
    }
  }
</style>
